  "starterCode": "# RoPE Freqs — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(seq_len, head_dim, theta=10000.0):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **RoPE Freqs** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(seq_len, head_dim, theta=10000.0):\n    if head_dim <= 0 or head_dim % 2: raise ValueError(\"head_dim must be positive and even\")\n    inv = 1.0 / (theta ** (np.arange(0, head_dim, 2, dtype=float) / head_dim))\n    pos = np.arange(seq_len, dtype=float)[:, None]\n    angles = pos * inv[None, :]\n    return {\"cos\": np.cos(angles).tolist(), \"sin\": np.sin(angles).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
